+## Keys and roles
+
+Every request sends `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. The key's role decides
+what it may do:
+
+| role      | may                                                              |
+|-----------|------------------------------------------------------------------|
+| `viewer`  | every GET except `GET /audit`                                    |
+| `cook`    | as viewer, plus `POST /recipes/:id/cook`, `POST /batches/:id/waste`, `POST /temperatures`, `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts` |
+| `manager` | everything, including `GET /audit`                               |
+
+- No key, a malformed header or an unknown key: 401 `unauthorized` (with
+  `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`). This is checked before the route, so unknown
+  routes also answer 401 without a key.
+- A known key whose role does not allow the route: 403 `forbidden`.
+
+## Audit
+
+Every request other than GET made with a known key adds an audit entry
+`{ id, at, keyName, method, path, status }`, whether it succeeded or not
+(so denied attempts show up as 403). `GET /audit` lists the entries newest
+first. Keys themselves are never logged or returned.
+
